lessons learned after creating conkys with a monospace font

::::: borders
- ${goto} add the +1px bug
- be consistent, use multiples of 6 for offsets
- ${alignr} offset depends on what background approach you are using in order
  for the characters from left to rigth to align
  conky adds 1px to the defined width, so 203 becomes 204

    vanilla bg, ie. a simple window with no fancy image just a solid color
    use desired width -1 for the setting
    alignr requires -1 as well
    otherwise you end up with a window 1px fatter than what you want

    complex bg, ie. image with shadow
    to keep things simple, have your image width be a multiple of 6\
    set the image to be desired width
    conky will add the extra pixel
    the ${alignr 6} will work as intended

